Can't decode camera previews and lossless JPEG frames in our image service

Our image service uses `purejsimage` for previews and for reading stored samples from `DICOM` images. We need the `HEVC` decoding path behind experimental `HEIC`, plus JPEG codestream inspection and lossless JPEG decoding, so these inputs can use the existing image workflows. For example, our frame reader calls:

```ts
import { decodeJpegLosslessFrame } from './src/codecs/jpeg-lossless.ts'
import { inspectJpegCodestream } from './src/codecs/jpeg.ts'
function openStoredFrame(frameBytes: Uint8Array) {
  const info = inspectJpegCodestream(frameBytes)
  return { info, frame: decodeJpegLosslessFrame(frameBytes, { requiredSelection: 1 }) }
}
```

I expect inspection metadata and decoded stored samples as described by the existing interfaces. Instead, these calls reach `throw new Error("not implemented")`; the `HEVC` context and residual paths have the same problem.

The missing implementations are in `src/codecs/hevc-cabac.ts`, `src/codecs/hevc-contexts.ts`, `src/codecs/hevc-residual.ts`, `src/codecs/jpeg-baseline.ts`, and `src/codecs/jpeg-lossless.ts`, along with the fixture encoder in `tests/dicom/jpeg-lossless-encode.ts`.

Please fill in these pieces following the existing doc comments where present and the declarations and conventions in `FEATURE.md`. The `README.md`’s “Support boundaries” section describes the codec scope. Keep the package’s own tests passing and preserve exported names and runtime beh
